What differs: in the design card (440×275), the dark bars hit and clip at the right edge from the fourth row down, and the last row is cut off at the bottom — it reads as an overflowing crop. The screenshot (960×400) shows all nine rows fully contained, with the longest bar stopping around two-thirds of the width and even vertical rhythm throughout.

So the screenshot is a faithful, uncropped rendering of the same design; the deviation is containment and row count visible, not styling. If the design intends edge-bleed bars, that's the one real mismatch.

